x_K = y_K\prod_{m> M}y_m^{\lfloor m/K\rfloor}\leqslant \Big(y_K^K\cdot\prod_{m> M}y_m^m\Big)^{1/K}\leqslant n^{1/K}\leqslant X^{\varepsilon/2}.
\end{align*}

\label{prop:DiophantineReduction}



Let $\alpha,\beta,\gamma\in (0,1]$ be fixed and let $X\geqslant 2$. For any $\varepsilon>0$ there exists an integer $d=d(\varepsilon)\geqslant 1$ such that the following holds.
