\end{align*}
where $d=\lfloor 10\varepsilon^{-4}\rfloor$ and $1\leqslant c_1,c_2,c_3\leqslant X^{\varepsilon^2/4}$. Since $(a,b,c)$ is counted by $S^*_{\alpha,\beta,\gamma}(X)$, we have $\gcd(a,b,c)=1$ and $a+b=c$, so $a,b,c$ are pairwise coprime. Hence, all the $3d+3$ numbers $x_i,y_i,z_i,c_1,c_2,c_3$ are pairwise coprime. Note also that by the properties of the factorisation given by Lemma~\ref{lem:DiophantineFactor}, we have
